{
  "info": {
    "name": "fastapi-blog API",
    "_postman_id": "b1f2c3d4-5e6f-4a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d",
    "description": "The JSON API behind called_mad.\n\nEvery request asserts the behaviour the routers document, not just the status code: PATCH leaves absent fields alone, PUT replaces everything, tags are normalised and replaced wholesale, a second DELETE is a 404, and a duplicate username is a 400 rather than a 500.\n\nThe run is self-contained. It creates its own user, works through that user's post, and deletes the user at the end - the cascade takes the post with it - so it can be run repeatedly against the same database without leaving anything behind.\n\nRun it from the repository root with `./scripts/api-tests.sh`, which starts the app against a throwaway database first. Against an already-running server, point the `baseUrl` environment variable at it.\n\nKnown contract wart: `date_posted` comes back with a `Z` suffix from POST /api/posts and without one everywhere else, because on create the value is still the timezone-aware object in memory while every other route reads it back from SQLite, which stores it naive. The tests assert only that it parses, so they stay green either way.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Contract",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "OpenAPI spec is reachable and complete",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/openapi.json",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "openapi.json"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The spec is generated by FastAPI from the routers, so it is the one description of this API that cannot drift from the code. The second test fails when an endpoint is added without a request in this collection - the collection is meant to cover the whole surface, and silence is how that stops being true."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const spec = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"spec exposes paths and schemas\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(spec).to.have.property(\"paths\");",
                  "    pm.expect(spec).to.have.property(\"components\");",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const documented = Object.keys(spec.paths).sort();",
                  "const covered = [\"/api/users\", \"/api/users/{user_id}\", \"/api/users/{user_id}/posts\", \"/api/posts\", \"/api/posts/{post_id}\", \"/api/tags\", \"/api/tags/{tag}/posts\"].sort();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"every documented endpoint is covered by this collection\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(documented, \"undocumented drift - add requests for the new paths\")",
                  "        .to.eql(covered);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": "Checks the API's own description before anything is exercised against it."
    },
    {
      "name": "Users",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create user",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates the user the rest of the run hangs off. The name carries a timestamp so the collection can be run repeatedly against the same database.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{newUsername}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{newEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"correct-horse-battery\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Unique per run, so re-running against a persistent database does not",
                  "// collide with the user the previous run left behind.",
                  "const stamp = Date.now();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"newUsername\", `pm_user_${stamp}`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"newEmail\", `pm_user_${stamp}@example.com`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201 Created\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "",
                  "const user = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"echoes what was sent\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(user.username).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"newUsername\"));",
                  "    pm.expect(user.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"newEmail\"));",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"id is a number\", () => pm.expect(user.id).to.be.a(\"number\"));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"falls back to the default avatar\", () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(user.image_path).to.eql(\"/static/profile_pics/avatar-256.jpg\"));",
                  "",
                  "// The response model is UserResponse, which has no password field at all.",
                  "// Asserted anyway: this is the one leak that would matter, and a response",
                  "// model is easy to widen by accident.",
                  "pm.test(\"never returns the password or its hash\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(user).to.not.have.property(\"password\");",
                  "    pm.expect(user).to.not.have.property(\"password_hash\");",
                  "    pm.expect(JSON.stringify(user)).to.not.include(\"correct-horse-battery\");",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"userId\", user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create user - duplicate is rejected",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "username and email are unique. The route checks first and also catches the IntegrityError, so a duplicate is a 400 rather than the 500 a raw constraint violation would give.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{newUsername}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{newEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"correct-horse-battery\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"400 Bad Request\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"says which rule was broken\", () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().detail).to.eql(\"Username or email already registered\"));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"detail is a string, not a validation array\", () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().detail).to.be.a(\"string\"));"
